      "side": 1,
      "message": "The argument order here leads to reversed \"Want\" and \"Got\" labels.\n\nStandard convention (and most GN tests) use `EXPECT_EQ(expected, actual)`.\nIf `a` is expected and `b` is actual:\n`got` becomes `expected`.\n`want` becomes `actual`.\nThe output below becomes:\n`Want: [actual]`\n`Got: [expected]`\n\nThis should be:\n`return base::StringPrintf(\"Want:\\n%s\\nGot:\\n%s\", got.data(), want.data());`\n(And the parameters to `DiffStrings` should probably be renamed to `expected, actual` to match).",
      "range": {
