      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is also reversed. `git diff` shows changes from the first file to the second.\nIf we want to see how the output (`actual`) differs from the baseline (`expected`), we should do `git diff expected actual`.\n\nCurrently:\n`want_path` has `actual`.\n`got_path` has `expected`.\n`git diff want_path got_path` results in `git diff actual expected`.\n\nThis should be:\n`cmdline.AppendArgPath(got_path);`\n`cmdline.AppendArgPath(want_path);`\n(Assuming `got` is renamed to `expected` and `want` is renamed to `actual`).",
      "range": {
